From: Gustavo Garcia <44309076+ElGuslml@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: enable sampleRateShading when the device supports it

NativeXRenderer's patch for its D138. The ReXGlue SDK's SPIR-V translator
writes a shader's alpha to coverage through gl_SampleMask, and only when the
device has sample rate shading (SampleMask depends on the SampleRateShading
capability in some SPIR-V revisions): without the feature, an Xbox 360
shader's alpha to coverage on a single-sampled target was left off instead of
the console's 2x2 dither. The feature is enabled where the GPU has it, as
robustBufferAccess is (patch 0001); NativeXRenderer reads it from the physical
device to configure the translator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Graphics/GraphicsEngineVulkan/src/EngineFactoryVk.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Graphics/GraphicsEngineVulkan/src/EngineFactoryVk.cpp b/Graphics/GraphicsEngineVulkan/src/EngineFactoryVk.cpp
index e58c0c6..20636e5 100644
--- a/Graphics/GraphicsEngineVulkan/src/EngineFactoryVk.cpp
+++ b/Graphics/GraphicsEngineVulkan/src/EngineFactoryVk.cpp
@@ -893,6 +893,9 @@ void EngineFactoryVkImpl::CreateDeviceAndContextsVk(const EngineVkCreateInfo& En
         // NativeXRenderer) read memory at addresses the application does not control; out-of-range reads must
         // return zero instead of faulting the device.
         vkEnabledFeatures.robustBufferAccess = vkDeviceFeatures.robustBufferAccess;
+        // Sample rate shading: translated shaders write a sample mask with it (an Xbox 360 shader's alpha to
+        // coverage in NativeXRenderer).
+        vkEnabledFeatures.sampleRateShading = vkDeviceFeatures.sampleRateShading;
         vkEnabledFeatures.drawIndirectFirstInstance               = vkDeviceFeatures.drawIndirectFirstInstance;
         vkEnabledFeatures.shaderStorageImageMultisample           = vkDeviceFeatures.shaderStorageImageMultisample;
         vkEnabledFeatures.shaderStorageImageReadWithoutFormat     = vkDeviceFeatures.shaderStorageImageReadWithoutFormat;
